    {
      "term": "YH Trade Union Incident",
      "matchText": "YH Trading Company",
      "definition": "The YH Trade Incident of August 1979: roughly 170 women workers at the YH Trading Company, a wig-and-textile exporter facing closure, occupied the opposition party's headquarters in protest. Riot police stormed the building in a pre-dawn raid, during which a young worker fell to her death. The brutality of the raid detonated public anger and fed the Busan-Masan demonstrations that destabilized the Park regime in its final months."
    },
    {
      "term": "Kim Kyung-suk",
      "matchText": "Kim Kyung-suk",
      "definition": "Kim Kyung-suk was the young female textile worker who died during the police raid that broke up the YH Trading Company sit-in in August 1979. Her death made her a martyr of the Korean labor movement and a catalyst for the anti-Yushin protests that swept Busan and Masan that autumn, weeks before President Park Chung-hee was assassinated."
    }
